# Line endings are part of the shipped artifact here, not a cosmetic choice.
#
# plugins/goodvibes/ARTIFACTS.json hashes every committed file under the plugin
# tree, and CI diffs a freshly rebuilt manifest against the committed one. On a
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) the working tree would
# hold CRLF copies, so a contributor regenerating the manifest there would hash
# different bytes for almost every text file and have it rejected by the Linux
# dist-match job with nothing local to explain the failure. Pinning the working
# tree to LF on every platform keeps those hashes machine-independent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# WASM payloads are copied byte for byte by the build. They must never be
# eol-converted, and diffing them as text is useless.
*.wasm binary

# The server bundles are generated build output, not hand-edited source:
# suppress whitespace warnings and collapse them in review by default.
plugins/goodvibes/server/**/index.cjs -whitespace linguist-generated
